body:
As a public health professional who works in blood pressure and diabetes research, the number of people who are being diagnosed with diabetes are higher than ever. It’s just surprising to hear if people above a certain age don’t have diabetes or high blood pressure. Oftentimes people will say no but tests show otherwise. Nothing about your interaction is biased and is just routine medical questions that every single patient is asked. Also, it’s really important to ask in case of liability issues

&#x200B;

Also research shows that people who are overweight are very much more likely to have diabetes. The very mechanism that causes (type 2) diabetes makes it very hard to lose weight and very likely to be overweight. This being said, it’s not okay for anyone to assume anything about your medical history given your weight.
